---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — ShiftCal"
  description="ShiftCal's privacy policy: calculations stay in your browser, no accounts, no server-side storage of your dates. Details on analytics and advertising cookies."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: August 15, 2026</em></p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    ShiftCal has no accounts and no databases of user data. The dates and pay rates you enter are
    processed entirely in your browser and are never transmitted to us. The only data written to
    your device is a small browser storage entry that remembers your own settings for your next
    visit, which you can clear at any time from your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No names, emails, or account credentials — there is nothing to sign up for.</li>
    <li>No schedule data: anchor dates, shift times, and pay rates stay on your device.</li>
    <li>No sale or sharing of personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use privacy-preserving, cookie-free aggregate analytics (page views, country, referrer) to
    understand which tools are useful. These analytics do not identify you or track you across
    other sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    ShiftCal is supported by advertising served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use
    cookies or device identifiers to serve ads, including personalized ads where you have
    consented. You can control ad personalization at
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, and learn how
    Google uses data from partner sites at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
      policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. Visitors in the EEA/UK are shown a
    consent dialog before any personalized advertising cookies are set.
  </p>

  <h2>ICS calendar exports</h2>
  <p>
    Calendar files are generated in your browser and downloaded directly to your device — the
    events in them never pass through our servers.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>ShiftCal is a workplace tool intended for adults and does not knowingly collect information from children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes to this policy will be reflected on this page with an updated date. Questions?
    Reach us via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
